# FULL JOB. profile=epson, cp=858 (the default), cut=none, feed=0
# body: printText(12, "none", false, "é")   -- a single e acute
# The ESC t byte and the encoded text are asserted TOGETHER in one vector. A right bytes /
# wrong ESC t pair is the classic "prints A-tilde-c instead of e acute" bug and is invisible
# to any test that checks only the text bytes.
1B 40      # ESC @      initialise
1B 74 13   # ESC t 19   code page 19 = PC858 Euro
1B 52 00   # ESC R 0    international character set 0
1B 61 00   # ESC a 0    justification left
1B 21 00   # ESC ! 0    print mode reset
1D 61 00   # GS a 0     disable automatic status back
82         # e acute at 0x82 in CP858 (encoder IBM00858)
